/-
# The Neggers–Stanley poset conjecture (Stanley, Problem 20)

R. P. Stanley, Positivity Problems and Conjectures in Algebraic Combinatorics, Problem 20: for a
finite poset `P` with linear extensions `𝓛(P)` (words in the labels), let `W(P, x) = ∑_{w ∈ 𝓛(P)}
x^{d(w)}`, `d(w)` the number of descents. Is every zero of `W(P, x)` real? (Conjectured by Neggers
for naturally labeled posets and extended by Stanley to all labelings.)
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import MathlibExt.Algebra.Polynomial.RealRooted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.Combinatorics.NeggersStanleyPosetConjectureAMR156Problem0020Wanted

/-!
Source: R. P. Stanley, Positivity Problems and Conjectures in Algebraic Combinatorics (1999),
Problem 20 (Neggers–Stanley conjecture). UnsolvedMath record UM-00801194 (`AMR-156-0020`), dataset
ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The poset lives on the labels `Fin n` and is given by a relation `R` (`R i j` meaning `i <_P j`)
with `R i j → i < j`, i.e. the labeling is natural; linear extensions of `R` and of its transitive
closure coincide, so transitivity is not imposed. The natural-labeling case is Neggers' original
conjecture; refuting it refutes Stanley's extension to arbitrary labelings. A linear extension is a
permutation `w` (the word `w 0, …, w (n - 1)`) with `w a` before `w b` whenever `R (w a) (w b)`, and
`d(w)` counts the `i` with `w i > w (i + 1)`. `W(P, x)` is nonzero (the identity is a linear
extension), so real-rootedness is `Polynomial.IsRealRooted` (MathlibExt) of its image in `ℂ[x]`.
Stembridge's `W_P(t) = ∑ t^{d(w)+1}` differs by the factor `t`.
-/

/-- The number of descents `d(w) = #{i : w i > w (i + 1)}` of a permutation `w` of `Fin n`, read as
the word `w 0, w 1, …, w (n - 1)`. -/
def descentCount {n : ℕ} (w : Equiv.Perm (Fin n)) : ℕ :=
  (Finset.univ.filter fun i : Fin n => ∃ h : i.val + 1 < n, w ⟨i.val + 1, h⟩ < w i).card

open Classical in
/-- The `W`-polynomial `W(P, x) = ∑_{w ∈ 𝓛(P)} x^{d(w)}` of the poset `P` on the labels `Fin n`
generated by the relation `R` (`R i j` meaning `i <_P j`). A linear extension is a word `w` listing
every label once with `w a` before `w b` whenever `R (w a) (w b)`; linear extensions of `R` and of
its transitive closure coincide, so `R` need not be transitive. -/
noncomputable def wPolynomial {n : ℕ} (R : Fin n → Fin n → Prop) : Polynomial ℤ :=
  ∑ w : Equiv.Perm (Fin n) with ∀ a b, R (w a) (w b) → a < b, Polynomial.X ^ descentCount w

/-- Neggers' conjecture (Stanley, Positivity Problems, Problem 20, for naturally labeled posets):
if `P` is naturally labeled (`i <_P j` implies `i < j`), every zero of `W(P, x)` is real. -/
def neggersConjecture : Prop :=
  ∀ (n : ℕ) (R : Fin n → Fin n → Prop), (∀ i j, R i j → i < j) →
    ((wPolynomial R).map (Int.castRingHom ℂ)).IsRealRooted

/--
Resolved false: Stembridge found naturally labeled posets on `17` elements whose `W`-polynomials
have non-real zeros, disproving Neggers' conjecture and hence the Neggers–Stanley conjecture
(Brändén had earlier given counterexamples with non-natural labelings). Source: R. P. Stanley,
Positivity Problems and Conjectures in Algebraic Combinatorics (1999), Problem 20 (Neggers–Stanley
conjecture); resolution: J. R. Stembridge, Counterexamples to the poset conjectures of Neggers,
Stanley, and Stembridge, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 359 (2007), 1115-1128; P. Brändén, Counterexamples
to the Neggers-Stanley conjecture, Electron. Res. Announc. Amer. Math. Soc. 10 (2004), 155-158
(non-natural labelings), Stembridge, Introduction: there exist naturally labeled narrow posets on 17
vertices whose W-polynomials have non-real zeros (and none smaller), disproving Neggers' original
conjecture; Figure 1 gives one, with W-polynomial t + 32t² + 336t³ + 1420t⁴ + 2534t⁵ + 1946t⁶ +
658t⁷ + 86t⁸ + 3t⁹, https://websites.umich.edu/~jrs/papers/pocon.pdf.
-/
public theorem_wanted neggersConjecture_refuted : ¬ neggersConjecture

end MathlibExt.Combinatorics.NeggersStanleyPosetConjectureAMR156Problem0020Wanted
